7. Correlation with CITEgeist performance gap
======================================================================

   Cell Type             % Unknown  Prot GT r   RNA GT r        Δ r
   ------------------------------------------------------------
   B cells                    1.6%       0.70       0.64      -0.06
   T cells                    6.5%       0.65       0.69      +0.04
   Macrophages               18.5%       0.75       0.66      -0.09
   Endothelial               13.4%       0.65       0.50      -0.15
   Epithelial                54.3%       0.60       0.54      -0.06
   Fibroblasts               39.3%       0.50       0.43      -0.07

======================================================================
CONCLUSION
======================================================================

If high '% Unknown' correlates with negative Δr (CITEgeist worse on RNA GT),
this confirms the hypothesis: cells that are protein-low but RNA-classifiable
create a disadvantage for CITEgeist when evaluated against RNA GT.

